    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup is anchored by **Bryce Harper** (78.75) and **Justin Crawford** (73.40), both of whom benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Max Scherzer (5.31 xERA). **Bryce Harper** is our primary engine today; his score is buoyed by an elite BvP track record, a wind-aided park boost, and the protection of the #3 spot in the order. Similarly, **Justin Crawford** is a priority start as his elite speed profile maximizes our scarcest category, SB, while the projected wind out at the park elevates his efficiency. We are also leaning into **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.65) and **Daulton Varsho** (63.69), as both possess strong platoon advantages against their respective right-handed opponents. While **Daulton Varsho** faces a tougher matchup against Michael King, his ability to contribute across the board\u2014despite the slight penalty for King\u2019s elite hold percentage\u2014keeps him as a locked-in starter.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Gavin Sheets**, who posted a respectable 49.20 score but was squeezed out by the efficiency of our MI/UTIL slots. While **Gavin Sheets** benefits from a dynamic platoon edge against Peter Lambert, **Jonathan Aranda** (58.01) and **Tyler Freeman** (50.19) provided better balance in the utility and middle infield spots, particularly given **Jonathan Aranda**'s projected #2 spot in the order. Caution is advised regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for both **Cal Raleigh** and **Jonathan Aranda**; if either falls lower in the batting order than the assumed #8 and #2 positions, respectively, their efficiency scores will crater. Furthermore, we are keeping a close eye on **Lawrence Butler** (53.15), whose score is suppressed by a negative platoon differential against Bennett, making him a candidate to be swapped if defensive substitutions or late lineup adjustments emerge.",
